WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.663
Choose the media route by the editing job.

2
00:00:02.863 --> 00:00:10.070
ClipSplat can record or import clips, add illustrated panels or image cards and cut sections.

3
00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:16.511
VideoSplat provides richer timeline work, named markers, captions and privacy tools.

4
00:00:16.711 --> 00:00:21.526
MediaSplat is useful for splitting, trimming and joining audio or video.

5
00:00:21.726 --> 00:00:25.308
AudioSplat records and edits multitrack audio.

6
00:00:25.508 --> 00:00:30.369
You may need only one or two of these tools for a short classroom explanation.

7
00:00:30.569 --> 00:00:32.893
Write the script before recording.

8
00:00:33.093 --> 00:00:38.700
Name the intended audience and keep the claim, evidence and limitation easy to follow.

9
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.158
A chart should remain readable in the exported frame.

10
00:00:42.358 --> 00:00:48.297
Use media you are allowed to reuse and avoid identifiable student information during practice.

11
00:00:48.497 --> 00:00:55.195
An equivalent slide-and-text response can meet the learning goal when recording is not accessible or appropriate.

12
00:00:55.395 --> 00:01:00.260
After export, inspect captions for names, numbers and timing.

13
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:06.899
Provide the transcript beside the video and describe visual evidence that the audio does not convey.

14
00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:11.363
Test the result with sound off and in another player if available.

15
00:01:11.563 --> 00:01:18.710
The course mini-lessons model a narrated slide format with local captions and transcripts; they are not live

16
00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:21.969
recordings of someone editing inside the apps.
